# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the thread tests, used by the
# "Thread Sanitizer" job in .github/workflows/build.yml:
#
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=$PWD/tsan.supp" make -C tests/thread Test
#
# Keep this list short.  Every entry is something a test does on purpose,
# never a race in the runtime; fix those instead.
#
# stress.icn is not listed here: its interference threads assign shared
# globals with no lock, on purpose, so it reports races in the
# assignment and dereference code that are the program's, not the
# runtime's.  The job runs it but does not check its log.

# misuse.icn unlocks a mutex it does not hold, and waits on a condition
# variable without its mutex, to check that unlock() and wait() fail with
# an error.  The runtime's mutexes are error-checking, so the pthread
# calls return EPERM, but TSan reports the attempts.
mutex:unlock_mutexid
mutex:Zwait
